      "correct_answer": 0,
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Reflect $A(1, 2)$ across the x-axis to $A'(1, -2)$. The line joining $A'$ and $(5, 3)$ has equation $y + 2 = \\frac{3 - (-2)}{5 - 1}(x - 1) = \\frac{5}{4}(x - 1)$. Setting $y = 0 \\implies 2 = \\frac{5}{4}(x - 1) \\implies x - 1 = 8/5 \\implies x = 13/5$."
